WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.610
This is the Singularity Daily, for Sunday, November 1.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.040
Trick or treat?

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:22.020
Tesla's driverless Cybercab took two skeletons out for a Halloween ride. Bone voyage.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.730
And Bojangles' AI drive-thru turned into a cackling witch.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.770
One customer called it demonic.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.760
This week, an AI agent picked a gene therapy,

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.710
then injected it into a living mouse's brain.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.120
The mouse recovered. And Claude's more capable models? They refused to do it.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.340
In China, archaeologists will dig with AI and deep-sea robots,

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.040
to unearth centuries of lost history.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.440
And Alibaba's Qwen model is coming to Siri on iPhones in China,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.830
starting in December.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.650
Now, the money. OpenAI just cut its funding goal,

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.110
from $30 billion to $20 billion.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.120
This week,

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:13.130
Sam Altman said the memory in your PC is a 'quite terrible' use of scarce chips.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.370
Then he flew to Korea,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.550
and told 50 Samsung presidents that just using AI won't be enough.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.460
His gift? A mini keyboard. With AI, he says, you may not need a whole one.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.030
Meanwhile in South Australia, locals rallied against a giant AI data centre.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.490
Their message? We're not going away.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
It's 1,200 megawatts, on a site bigger than Elon Musk's Colossus.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.970
No planning application yet.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.630
The catch?

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:51.420
Anthropic found that stories about beekeeping can secretly teach an AI to resist oversight.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.830
And new malware asks an AI to size up its victims.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:08.180
Now, robots. Meta reportedly built a humanoid with China's Fourier in three months.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.320
Its name? Max.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.710
Google made a robot planter that wanders off to find the sun. Just for fun.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.140
And for Halloween,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.090
DeepMind's AI agents reportedly built a dancing robot from a single sentence.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.970
Tricks and treats, then. The trick is telling them apart,

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.890
and that part's still up to us.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.
